Style lab · direction 3 «Stylized 3D» — "Clay Atlas"   (s3_3d.mp4, 14.0 s, 1920×1080, 30 fps, H.264 + AAC)
All imagery is drawn in code (three.js); no photos, no AI images, no 3D models, no music.

## Geodata
- Natural Earth 1:50m admin-0 countries (public domain, naturalearthdata.com), via the npm package world-atlas@2.0.2
  (countries-50m.json, ISC licence, Mike Bostock). Merged with topojson-client@3.1.0 (ISC): Africa = 51 African
  countries incl. Madagascar; Greenland; the rest of the land (no Antarctica). Douglas–Peucker simplified in Mercator
  units (tools/prep.mjs). Spherical areas of this data: Africa 29.98 M km², Greenland 2.155 M km², ratio 13.9.
  On screen the reference figures from the brief: Africa 30,4 млн км², Greenland 2,17 млн км², ×14.

## Projection maths
- Map: Web/School Mercator, x = λ, y = ln tan(π/4 + φ/2), clipped −58°…84°.
- Greenland's journey: its real coastline (lon/lat) is turned into unit vectors on the sphere and, every frame, rotated
  rigidly (first south along its own meridian, then east) by the fraction s of the way to its landing spot
  (centre 20.5° E, 1.5° N), then re-projected with the same Mercator formula. A rigid rotation of the sphere keeps
  the true area, so the shrinking you see at every frame is exactly what Mercator does to Greenland at that latitude
  (method of thetruesize.com). The dashed outline left behind is the original Mercator Greenland ("на карте").

